      <room>AW1.117</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>GNUstep on OpenBSD, a short overview</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>World of GNUstep devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will focus on what was there, half a year ago and what will OpenBSD 4.9 have in the ports tree. The following questions will be answered:&#xA;* why GNUstep on OpenBSD?&#xA;* what works (where, i.e. which platforms), and what&amp;#39;s not?&#xA;* why its not working on some platforms?&#xA;* what&amp;#39;s planned, or needed to have more progress/GNUstep ports added?&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will focus on what was there, half a year ago and what will OpenBSD 4.9 have in the ports tree. The following questions will be answered:&#xA;* why GNUstep on OpenBSD?&#xA;* what works (where, i.e. which platforms), and what&amp;#39;s not?&#xA;* why its not working on some platforms?&#xA;* what&amp;#39;s planned, or needed to have more progress/GNUstep ports added?&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1291">Sebastian Reitenbach</person>
      </persons>
